title: FortiBleed FortigateSniffer Artifact File Creation
id: 9c5075c2-b1fd-4e20-9a40-e10854a1e3e0
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects creation of the named artifacts of the FortiBleed credential theft
    campaign: the Go-based FortigateSniffer capture output fg_capture.log and
    the Active Directory enumeration scripts ad_enum.py and ad_full_audit.py
    dropped after admin access is obtained on Fortinet edge devices, alongside
    Hashcat and Hashtopolis cracking orchestration. Filenames are documented
    by Recorded Future and SOCRadar reporting on the campaign.
references:
    - https://cyberscoop.com/fortibleed-fortinet-vpn-ransomware-fbi-warning/
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/fortibleed-campaign-used-custom-fortigate-sniffer-to-steal-credentials/
    - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/large-scale-credential-attacks/
    - https://blog.qualys.com/vulnerabilities-threat-research/2026/07/08/fortibleed-fortigate-credential-reuse-internet-exposed
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026-10-07
tags:
    - attack.t1040
    - attack.t1070
logsource:
    category: file_event
detection:
    selection_artifact:
        TargetFilename|contains:
            - 'fg_capture.log'
            - 'ad_enum.py'
            - 'ad_full_audit.py'
    condition: selection_artifact
falsepositives:
    - Administrator or incident-response tooling that legitimately uses these script names
    - Unrelated packet-capture files named fg_capture.log
level: high
